_refine_special_details
;
 Refined as a 2-component twin,using a 2-fold rotation, which related the
 F centered orthorhombic cell to the I centered tetragonal. The BASF of
 0.424(10) indicates that the higher metric symmetry is not appropriate.
Hydrogen atoms were not found in the difference map, so were not refined
in the structure. 
The shape of the density in the Fobs maps indicated disorder in two out 
of the three iodine positions. The nearest, largest Q-peaks next to each
were refined as partialy occupied iodine sites. The ratio of occupancies
(major sites: minor sites)  was 3:1.  The occupancies were then fixed. 
An EADP was used between pairs of sites. 
The methylammonium was found in the difference map. The carbon and the 
nitrogen share the same position, and have been refined with EADP & EXYZ. 
A DFIX was used, to keep the site from collapsing into the center of the bond.
The DFIX value used was derived from the inital distance.
;
